WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
Germany, in the 1820s.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:07.210
A landowner's farms send their
produce overland to the market city.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.570
The landowner is Johann
Heinrich von Thünen.

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.650
In 1826, he publishes a book
called The Isolated State.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.390
His idea starts simply: one
city, alone on a flat plain,

6
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.290
with the same soil and climate everywhere.

7
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.840
Why would that one city decide what
every farm around it should grow?

8
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.850
In this mission, you'll build his
model, and work out where cattle,

9
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.430
grain, milk and wood belong.

10
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.130
Then you'll test it at bigger scales,
and find farms that break the pattern.

11
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.050
Your mission: explain how one city could
decide what every farm around it would

12
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.670
grow.
